    {
      "id": 161,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1850,
        6160
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# H3 Short Film - CHAIN RENDER (picture + sound carried between scenes)\n\nThe plain short-film workflow renders every scene as its own clip, and H3 invents each clip's sound from nothing - so at every scene change the room tone, the score and whatever was mid-air at the cut all restart. This variant renders the scenes **one after another inside one node** and pins the last `context_frames` of the previous scene's *sampled latent* - **picture and sound together** - to the head of the next scene, so both continue.\n\n1. Paste your **manuscript** into the **H3 Short Film Writer**. `continuity_mode` is set to **Continuous chain**: from scene 02 on, `[Shot 1]` opens on the last frame of the previous scene and each scene is one continuous take. `handoff_pass` (on) adds one LLM turn that rewrites any opening whose props, positions or light drift from the previous ending.\n2. The **Short Film Chain Render** replaces Ref2VA -> guider -> sampler -> decode -> Save Clip. `context_frames` snaps to the AV-aligned runs 39 (~1.6 s) / 90 (~3.75 s) / 141 (~5.9 s); `audio_feather_ticks` 8 = a 0.2 s release at the end of the inherited sound. Set `continuity` to *cut everywhere* to render independent clips again for comparison.\n3. Needs **ComfyUI-H3-Motion-Context-MultiRef** (its `MiniMaxH3GeneratedAVMaskedContext` does the latent copy). Without it only the picture is carried (core guide clip) and the report says so.\n4. Clips land under `output/video/<project>/H3_film_sNN...`; the node's `report` lists, per scene, whether it continued, the frames delivered (grid padding stays in the clip on purpose - the next scene continues from the latent's real tail) and the trimmed head.\n\nSet `width`/`height` on the Resolution Selector; they are wired into the render node."
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
